verdicts.evidence:
plannedTasks early-returns 0 whenever st.Tasks is non-empty without ever reading the index: `func plannedTasks(bdir string, st *bundle.State) int {
	if len(st.Tasks) > 0 {
		return 0
	}
	idx, err := readIndex(bdir)
...` (internal/cli/cmd_status.go:177-185). materialiseTasks (internal/cli/cmd_next.go:557-573) never deletes plan.index.json, and it is read throughout execute/finish by cmd_next.go, cmd_close_wave.go, cmd_verify.go, so a run with materialised tasks still has a readable index on disk — exactly the state that would hit this early return. No test asserts TasksPlanned==0 (JSON `tasks.planned`) or checks the absence of the 'planned (not yet materialised)' text line for a bundle with non-empty st.Tasks: the only assertions on the 'planned' field/text are in the new plan-phase test (cmd_status_test.go:415-425, tasks empty); reviewerRun-based tests (TestStatusInternalReviewLine/Skipped/ZeroCandidatesNotVerifyPending, all using the reviewerRun fixture that sets both st.Tasks and plan.index.json) only assert on 'internal review: ...' substrings via strings.Contains, never on the tasks/planned line; and execute_test.go:254 only reads `tasks.items`, never `tasks.total` or `tasks.planned`. So the materialised-tasks early-return branch is exercised by existing fixtures but never checked by any assertion.
